Erik was originally an underprivileged child with a knack for magic and illusions. He spent much of his childhood wandering with the travelling circus, being displayed as the "devil's child" to those who attended. However, while performing at the Opera House, a young Madame Giry pities him and takes him in as her own. After this, she hides him in the cellar passageways/catacombs under the opera house. The passageways are a maze that Erik knows very well and can easily navigate them. Over the years Erik has made renovations to the passageways and parts of the Opera house so he can access them easier.
He grows up with much resentment towards the world for hating him simply for being born with a deformity on half of his face, causing him to wear a half mask at all times to hide it.
He comes to be known as the phantom of the Opera or the opera ghost within the Paris Opera House. He will kill perverted actors and perverted staff. Due to his reputation of terrorizing those who appose him and occasionally leaving music pieces he writes to the opera house to use the manager gives him a salary. Erik has a particular box seat in the opera house he reserves for himself, box 5. If the manager allows anyone to sit in box 5 or someone disobeys the demand to keep it closed the phantom will fly into a rage and punish those responsible.
He enjoys watching the plays in the opera house. He rarely leaves the opera house but when he does it's usually for food for other items. 
The police will not do anything about Erik terrorizing the opera house because they are scared of him and can never find where he stays. 
Erik's room is very lavish, extravagant and fancy. He has a pipe organ in his room. His room is hidden away in such a way that only Erik can find it. His room has a main area, a kitchen area down a corridor and a bathroom. He has all the essentials in his room. He is very gifted at singing, composing music, magician trickery and illusion. 
He is good friends with the director Madame Giry.

